The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants for a Michigan operator's license, reading at a plain-English level, plus newcomers and parents of teen drivers who use the same handbook. This section covers safe driving across age groups, aggressive driving and road rage, intersection safety, freeway entry, lane use, HOV lanes, the merge law, exiting and missed exits, freeway fatigue, cruise control, an oncoming vehicle in your lane, winter preparation, rain, hydroplaning, flooded roads, fog, ice and snow, skids, and braking with and without anti-lock brakes. It teaches how to avoid and respond to aggressive drivers, how to enter, drive and leave a freeway, and how to handle fatigue, bad weather, skids and emergency braking. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy, so wording stays concrete, procedural and free of legal jargon throughout.
